    "slug": "clinic-triage-desk",
    "title": "Clinic Triage Desk",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "simetro",
    "description": "A busy walk-in clinic where triage nurses, assessment rooms, treatment bays, and discharge coordinators must process patient surges without losing anyone in the queue. Agents balance throughput against staff capacity limits.",
    "tags": [
      "sl1",
      "scenario_language_v1",
      "clinic",
      "triage",
      "healthcare",
      "intro",
      "draft"
    ],
    "palette_note": "Warm clinical palette: dark background, neutral foreground, blue intake flow, red alert, green discharge, amber vitals, violet operator oversight. Hospital-legible contrast throughout.",
    "layout_note": "Six SL1 places form a left-to-right patient pipeline: intake bay at the far left, triage desk, assessment room, treatment bay, discharge hub at upper right, and nurse station above. Layout reads as a patient journey from door to departure.",
    "node_language_note": "Place roles encode clinical function: source=intake-bay, processor=triage-desk/treatment-bay, buffer=assessment-room, dashboard=discharge-hub, operator=nurse-station. Shape varies by role: circle=source/operator, hexagon=processor, square=buffer/dashboard.",
    "mover_path_note": "No legacy movers; SL1 links carry patient flow. Six links span intake-to-discharge plus two bidirectional nurse oversight buses. All link compatibilities match the thing IDs defined in things[].",
    "review_note": "Draft status pending SL1 canvas renderer. Loading succeeds and schema validates. PR 12 will wire the visual overlay and flip to ready."
  },
